\ cv8-save.4 - SAVE-SYSTEM writing a CV8 image.
\
\ The last piece of phase 3: a CV8 system that can save itself, with no
\ cell image and no translator in the loop. Load after save-system.4
\ (and after cv8.4); --cv8-compiler swaps `SAVE-SYSTEM8` into
\ `SAVE-SYSTEM` and `SS-SET-MAGIC8` into `SS-SET-MAGIC`.
\
\ The only real difference from the cell version is the header. A cell
\ image is 8 magic bytes then the dictionary; a CV8 image is
\ (CV8-REFERENCE.md 5.1):
\
\     magic 8 bytes   "CV8" + scale digit, cell width, 'L', version, flags
\     head_nfa  cell  offset of the newest word's name field
\     ntails    cell  DOES> tail count - always 0 here, because DODOES
\                     carries its target inline (--dataprims)
\     locals    5 cells, present whenever the specialised opcodes are
\
\ Everything else - SS-SCRUB, the unrelocation, RESET-BUFFERS - is the
\ cell version's and is already right: it zeroes every cell holding a
\ live-session address, which is exactly what made TRANSLATED images
\ non-reproducible across dumps.

BASE @  DECIMAL

VARIABLE SS-HEAD        \ newest NFA, captured before SS-SCRUB clears LAST

: SS-SET-MAGIC8 ( --- )
  \ Must agree with the engine's IMAGE_MAGIC exactly, including the
  \ feature bits, or the image is refused at load.
  [CHAR] C SS-MAGIC     C!
  [CHAR] V SS-MAGIC 1+  C!
  [CHAR] 8 SS-MAGIC 2 + C!
  \ scale digit: 3 on a 64-bit cell, 2 on a 32-bit one
  48 CV8-SHIFT + SS-MAGIC 3 + C!
  1 CELLS  SS-MAGIC 4 + C!
  [CHAR] L SS-MAGIC 5 + C!      \ specialised opcodes present
  1        SS-MAGIC 6 + C!      \ format version
  15       SS-MAGIC 7 + C! ;    \ varcall | varslot | spec | lit64

: SS-CELL, ( n --- )
  \ Append one cell to the image file, reusing SS-MAGIC as scratch: the
  \ magic itself has already been written by then.
  SS-MAGIC ! SS-MAGIC 1 CELLS SS-FID @ WRITE-FILE DROP ;

: SS-HEADER, ( --- )
  \ The CV8 header fields that follow the magic.
  SS-HEAD @ SS-CELL,                    \ head_nfa
  0 SS-CELL,                            \ ntails: DODOES is self-contained
  LSAVE-SP    START @ - SS-CELL,        \ the locals save-stack pointer
  LSAVE-STACK START @ - SS-CELL,        \ and its buffer
  LSAVE-MAX             SS-CELL,        \ its limit
  ['] LSAVE     START @ - SS-CELL,      \ fallbacks, for the ABORT" paths
  ['] LRESTORE  START @ - SS-CELL, ;

: SAVE-SYSTEM8 ( c-addr u --- )
  RESET-BUFFERS
  HERE START @ - SS-LEN !
  SS-LEN @ ALLOCATE ABORT" SAVE-SYSTEM: out of memory" SS-BUF !
  START @ SS-BUF @ SS-LEN @ MOVE
  DP SS-UNRELOCATE
  FORTH-WORDLIST SS-UNRELOCATE
  \ The dictionary head. NOT LAST: a translated image never had LAST
  \ remapped, so it holds a stale address of the build session. The
  \ wordlist head is remapped, and is the same word.
  FORTH-WORDLIST @ START @ - SS-HEAD !
  SS-SCRUB
  SS-SET-MAGIC
  W/O BIN CREATE-FILE ABORT" SAVE-SYSTEM: cannot create file" SS-FID !
  SS-MAGIC 8 SS-FID @ WRITE-FILE DROP
  SS-HEADER,
  SS-BUF @ SS-LEN @ SS-FID @ WRITE-FILE DROP
  SS-FID @ CLOSE-FILE DROP
  SS-BUF @ FREE DROP ;

BASE !
